cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CIDM or build on its design, please cite it as below (and a GitHub star is appreciated)."
type: software
title: "Jev-Orchestrated Decision Mesh: Caber Interstitial Decision Mesh (CIDM)"
abstract: >-
  CIDM is a training-free orchestration design in which Jev, a typed decision
  model, governs a five-unit network of existing frontier models: it chooses
  each bounded operation, receives every completed unit output, and decides
  whether to forward, repair, escalate, retrieve evidence or request a separate
  check. Execution is bounded by single-use capability permits, spend caps,
  hash-linked journals and release audits. The repository contains the research
  thesis, the reference implementation and its recorded live evidence.
